   21:     question: 'Why is the famous Aranmula Kannadi metal mirror from Kerala unique compared to standard household glass mirrors?',
   22      options: [
   23:       'It is polished with liquid mercury and diamond dust',
   24:       'It is a front-surface reflecting alloy that eliminates secondary refraction and distortion',
   25:       'It can only be viewed under sunlight',
   26:       'It is crafted from translucent quartz crystal'
   27      ],
   28      correctAnswer: 1,
   29:     explanation: 'Standard glass mirrors have reflective silver coating on the rear, causing double-refraction and image distortion. Aranmula Kannadi is a 100% front-reflecting secret copper-tin alloy mirror with zero glass.',
   30      category: 'Traditional Science & Crafts',
   31:     verifiedSource: 'Geographical Indications Registry of India (GI #1)',
   32      xpReward: 50

   35      id: 'q3',
   36:     question: 'Which sacred textile from Gujarat requires both the warp and weft threads to be tie-dyed separately with micro-precision before weaving on the loom?',
   37      options: [
   38:       'Patan Patola (Double Ikat)',
   39        'Bandhani Tie-Dye',

   43      correctAnswer: 0,
